IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra1-ch3-general`
IMPORT `wra1-ch1-entitlement`

-- Tests for wra1-ch1-entitlement.l4 (sections 1 to 12). Every expected value is written by hand from the text quoted in the
-- module, beside the assertion. A number such as 100 is an invented test figure: the Act supplies none of these amounts.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, place IS A Place
GIVETH A Person
`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` MEANS Person WITH
    `reference` IS "T"
    `age in years` IS age
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2000     -- placeholder: no rule reads it
    `where the person is` IS place
    `where the person lives` IS place

GIVEN married IS A BOOLEAN, household IS A BOOLEAN, living IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Two people`
`s 1(2) test: two people` MEANS `Two people` WITH
    `the first person` IS `s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 30 Wales
    `the second person` IS `s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 31 Wales
    `their relationship` IS `Relationship of two people` WITH
        `married to each other or civil partners of each other` IS married
        `members of the same household` IS household
        `living together as if married or civil partners` IS living

`s 1(2) test: a single claimant` MEANS `a single claimant` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 30 Wales)
`s 1(2) test: joint claimants who are a couple` MEANS `joint claimants` (`s 1(2) test: two people` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
`s 1(2) test: joint claimants who are not a couple` MEANS `joint claimants` (`s 1(2) test: two people` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 1`

#ASSERT `s 1(1) the benefit payable in accordance with this Part` EQUALS `universal credit`
-- (2)(a) "an individual who is not a member of a couple (a 'single person')"
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(a) the individual is a single person` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(2)(a) the individual is a single person` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- (2)(a) a single claimant who is not a member of a couple
#ASSERT `s 1(2) universal credit may be awarded to these claimants` `s 1(2) test: a single claimant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a single claimant who is in fact a member of a couple needs s 2(2) regulations: not covered
#ASSERT `s 1(2) universal credit may be awarded to these claimants` `s 1(2) test: a single claimant` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(b) members of a couple jointly
#ASSERT `s 1(2) universal credit may be awarded to these claimants` `s 1(2) test: joint claimants who are a couple` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- two people who are not a couple: the text does not say they may not, so not covered
#ASSERT `s 1(2) universal credit may be awarded to these claimants` `s 1(2) test: joint claimants who are not a couple` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(a)-(d) the four elements
#ASSERT count `s 1(3) the elements by reference to which an award is calculated` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the section that gives the element` `s 1(3)(a) standard allowance` EQUALS "section 9"
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the section that gives the element` `s 1(3)(b) responsibility for children or young persons` EQUALS "section 10"
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the section that gives the element` `s 1(3)(c) housing` EQUALS "section 11"
#ASSERT `s 1(3) the section that gives the element` `s 1(3)(d) other particular needs or circumstances` EQUALS "section 12"

§ `s 2`

#ASSERT `s 2(1) a claim may be made by these claimants` `s 1(2) test: a single claimant` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) a claim may be made by these claimants` `s 1(2) test: joint claimants who are a couple` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) a claim may be made by these claimants` `s 1(2) test: a single claimant` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a member of a couple may make a claim as a single person` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a member of a couple may make a claim as a single person` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) a member of a couple may make a claim as a single person` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 3`

-- (1) "is entitled ... if the claimant meets (a) the basic conditions, and (b) the financial conditions"
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the single claimant is entitled to universal credit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the single claimant is entitled to universal credit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the single claimant is entitled to universal credit` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the single claimant is entitled to universal credit` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1) the single claimant is entitled to universal credit` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) "each of them meets the basic conditions" and "they meet the financial conditions for joint claimants"
#ASSERT `s 3(2) joint claimants are jointly entitled to universal credit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) joint claimants are jointly entitled to universal credit` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) joint claimants are jointly entitled to universal credit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) joint claimants are jointly entitled to universal credit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) joint claimants are jointly entitled to universal credit` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) joint claimants are jointly entitled to universal credit` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 4`

-- (1)(a) "is at least 18 years old": 18 is in, 17 is not (provisionally), s 4(3) regulations replace the minimum where supplied
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the person is at least 18 years old` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 18 Wales) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the person is at least 18 years old` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 17 Wales) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the person is at least 18 years old` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 17 Wales) (JUST 16) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the person is at least 18 years old` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 15 Wales) (JUST 16) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the person is at least 18 years old` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 20 Wales) (JUST 21) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the person is at least 18 years old` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 21 Wales) (JUST 21) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(b) "has not reached the qualifying age for state pension credit" (the fact is asked: s 4(4) points at another Act)
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(b) the person has not reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(b) the person has not reached the qualifying age for state pension credit` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- (1)(c) "is in Great Britain": the six places
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the place is in Great Britain` `Greater London` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the place is in Great Britain` `England outside Greater London` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the place is in Great Britain` Scotland EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the place is in Great Britain` Wales EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the place is in Great Britain` `Northern Ireland` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the place is in Great Britain` `outside the United Kingdom` EQUALS FALSE
-- (1)(c) with s 4(5)(a)-(b) regulations: supplied regulations override the place; none supplied means the place decides
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the person is in Great Britain` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 30 Wales) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the person is in Great Britain` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 30 `Northern Ireland`) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the person is in Great Britain` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 30 `outside the United Kingdom`) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the person is in Great Britain` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 30 `outside the United Kingdom`) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the person is in Great Britain` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 30 `outside the United Kingdom`) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(c) the person is in Great Britain` (`s 4(1)(a) test: a person of age in place` 30 Wales) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
-- (1)(d) "is not receiving education"; "receiving education" is for regulations (s 4(6))
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(d) the person is not receiving education` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(d) the person is not receiving education` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(d) the person is not receiving education` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(6)(b): regulations treat the person as not receiving education (JUST FALSE) or as receiving it (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(d) the person is not receiving education` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(d) the person is not receiving education` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(e) "has accepted a claimant commitment"; s 4(7) regulations may treat the person as having accepted or not
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(e) the person has accepted a claimant commitment` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(e) the person has accepted a claimant commitment` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(e) the person has accepted a claimant commitment` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(e) the person has accepted a claimant commitment` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(e) the person has accepted a claimant commitment` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) all five limbs
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one limb fails and no exception is known: the "no" is provisional (s 4(2))
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- one limb fails and the regulations say there is no exception: the definition says no
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- one limb fails and the regulations except the person: the other limbs are met
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an excepted failure does not cure a limb that is not known
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a limb that is not known, none known to fail
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- a failure with another limb unknown, the regulations saying no exception: still no
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- each limb failing alone, with no exception: five "no" answers
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the person meets the basic conditions` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 5`

-- (1)(a) "not greater than a prescribed amount": 100 against 100 is in, 101 is out
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(a) the claimant's capital is not greater than the prescribed amount` 100 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(a) the claimant's capital is not greater than the prescribed amount` 101 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(a) the claimant's capital is not greater than the prescribed amount` 0 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(a) the claimant's capital is not greater than the prescribed amount` 100 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b) "the amount payable would not be less than any prescribed minimum"
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` (JUST 10) (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` (JUST 9) (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` (JUST 11) (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` (JUST 10) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(1)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` NOTHING (JUST 10) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "are that (a) and (b)"
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the financial conditions for a single claimant are met` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the financial conditions for a single claimant are met` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the financial conditions for a single claimant are met` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) joint claimants: combined capital and combined income
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) their combined capital is not greater than the prescribed amount` 100 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) their combined capital is not greater than the prescribed amount` 101 (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) their combined capital is not greater than the prescribed amount` 1 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` (JUST 10) (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` (JUST 9) (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` NOTHING (JUST 10) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the amount payable would not be less than the prescribed minimum` (JUST 10) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(2) the financial conditions for joint claimants are met` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2) the financial conditions for joint claimants are met` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(2) the financial conditions for joint claimants are met` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 6`

-- (1)(a) prescribed circumstances apply: entitlement does not arise
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST TRUE) 30 (JUST 7) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (1)(b) "if the requirements in section 3 are met for a period shorter than a prescribed period": 6 days against 7, restricted
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST FALSE) 6 (JUST 7) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 7 days against 7 is not shorter: the "if" fails, and with the other limbs "no" the entitlement is not restricted
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST FALSE) 7 (JUST 7) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST FALSE) 8 (JUST 7) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(c) the person is within the prescribed period at the beginning
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST FALSE) 30 (JUST 7) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- limb (c) is not known, the others "no": not covered
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST FALSE) 30 (JUST 7) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- limb (b) is not known (no prescribed period), limb (c) restricts
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST FALSE) 30 NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- limb (a) is not known, the others "no"
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` NOTHING 30 (JUST 7) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6(3) exception: limbs (b) and (c) are removed
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST FALSE) 1 (JUST 7) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the exception does not reach limb (a)
#ASSERT `s 6(1) entitlement to universal credit does not arise` (JUST TRUE) 1 (JUST 7) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2) "may not exceed seven days": 7 in, 8 out
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the prescribed period is within the seven-day limit` (JUST 7) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the prescribed period is within the seven-day limit` (JUST 8) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the prescribed period is within the seven-day limit` (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the prescribed period is within the seven-day limit` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 7`

`s 7(1) test: the period of entitlement` MEANS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `last day` IS Date 31 12 2025
`s 7(1) test: an assessment period inside it` MEANS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 1 3 2025, `last day` IS Date 28 3 2025
`s 7(1) test: an assessment period equal to it` MEANS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `last day` IS Date 31 12 2025
`s 7(1) test: an assessment period starting a day early` MEANS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 31 12 2024, `last day` IS Date 27 1 2025
`s 7(1) test: an assessment period ending a day late` MEANS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 5 12 2025, `last day` IS Date 1 1 2026
`s 7(1) test: a four week assessment period` MEANS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2025, `last day` IS Date 28 1 2025
`s 7(1) test: a one day period` MEANS Period WITH `first day` IS Date 5 1 2025, `last day` IS Date 5 1 2025

-- (1) "each complete assessment period within a period of entitlement"
#ASSERT `s 7(1) universal credit is payable in respect of the assessment period` `s 7(1) test: an assessment period inside it` `s 7(1) test: the period of entitlement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(1) universal credit is payable in respect of the assessment period` `s 7(1) test: an assessment period equal to it` `s 7(1) test: the period of entitlement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(1) universal credit is payable in respect of the assessment period` `s 7(1) test: an assessment period starting a day early` `s 7(1) test: the period of entitlement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(1) universal credit is payable in respect of the assessment period` `s 7(1) test: an assessment period ending a day late` `s 7(1) test: the period of entitlement` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "a period of a prescribed duration": 1 to 28 January is 28 days, both ends counting
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the period is an assessment period` `s 7(1) test: a four week assessment period` (JUST 28) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the period is an assessment period` `s 7(1) test: a four week assessment period` (JUST 29) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the period is an assessment period` `s 7(1) test: a four week assessment period` (JUST 27) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the period is an assessment period` `s 7(1) test: a one day period` (JUST 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the period is an assessment period` `s 7(1) test: a four week assessment period` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) "period of entitlement" means a period during which entitlement subsists
#ASSERT `s 7(4) the period is a period of entitlement` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(4) the period is a period of entitlement` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `s 8`

-- (4) a single claimant's own income; joint claimants' combined income
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the income to which the deductions refer` `s 1(2) test: a single claimant` 100 50 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the income to which the deductions refer` `s 1(2) test: joint claimants who are a couple` 100 50 EQUALS 150
-- (2) the maximum amount is the total of the four amounts
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the sum of two possibly unknown amounts` (JUST 1) (JUST 2) EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the sum of two possibly unknown amounts` (JUST 1) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the sum of two possibly unknown amounts` NOTHING (JUST 2) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the maximum amount` (JUST 1) (JUST 2) (JUST 3) (JUST 4) EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the maximum amount` (JUST 1) (JUST 0) (JUST 0) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the maximum amount` (JUST 1) (JUST 2) NOTHING (JUST 4) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(2) the maximum amount` NOTHING (JUST 2) (JUST 3) (JUST 4) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(a)-(b) multiplying income by a prescribed percentage (here 50 per hundred)
#ASSERT `s 8(3)(a) the amount deducted in respect of earned income` 200 (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 8(3)(a) the amount deducted in respect of earned income` 200 (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 8(3)(a) the amount deducted in respect of earned income` 200 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(3)(b) the amount deducted in respect of unearned income` 80 (JUST 25) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 8(3)(b) the amount deducted in respect of unearned income` 80 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) the balance of the maximum amount less the amounts to be deducted
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` (JUST 500) (JUST 100) (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST 350
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` (JUST 500) (JUST 0) (JUST 0) EQUALS JUST 500
-- deductions that exceed the maximum amount: the Act says only "the balance", so the arithmetic balance is reported (fork F-8)
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` (JUST 100) (JUST 80) (JUST 50) EQUALS JUST (0 MINUS 30)
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` NOTHING (JUST 100) (JUST 50) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` (JUST 500) NOTHING (JUST 50) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` (JUST 500) (JUST 100) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 9`

-- (1) "is to include an amount by way of an allowance for (a) a single claimant, or (b) joint claimants"
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the calculation of the award includes the standard allowance` `s 1(2) test: a single claimant` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the calculation of the award includes the standard allowance` `s 1(2) test: joint claimants who are a couple` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
